.TH "libnvmf_insert_tls_key" 9 "libnvmf_insert_tls_key" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_insert_tls_key \- Derive and insert a TLS PSK
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "int" libnvmf_insert_tls_key
.BI "(struct libnvme_global_ctx *ctx "  ","
.BI "const char *keyring "  ","
.BI "const char *key_type "  ","
.BI "const char *hostnqn "  ","
.BI "const char *subsysnqn "  ","
.BI "enum libnvmf_hmac_alg hmac "  ","
.BI "unsigned char *configured_key "  ","
.BI "int key_len "  ","
.BI "long *key "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "ctx" 12
struct libnvme_global_ctx object
.IP "keyring" 12
Keyring to use
.IP "key_type" 12
Type of the resulting key
.IP "hostnqn" 12
Host NVMe Qualified Name
.IP "subsysnqn" 12
Subsystem NVMe Qualified Name
.IP "hmac" 12
HMAC algorithm
.IP "configured_key" 12
Configured PSK to derive the retained PSK from
.IP "key_len" 12
Length of \fIconfigured_key\fP
.IP "key" 12
Key serial to return
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Derives a retained PSK from \fIconfigured_key\fP and, from that, the TLS PSK
and its identity, using identity version 0, as specified in the NVMe
TCP Transport Specification 1.0, section 3.6.1.3. Stores the TLS PSK
as type \fIkey_type\fP under that identity in the keyring specified by
\fIkeyring\fP.

The NVMe TCP Transport Specification 1.3 marks identity version 0
obsolete. Use \fBlibnvmf_insert_tls_key_versioned\fP to select the
identity version.
.SH "RETURN"
0 on success, negative error code otherwise.
